CORE
main.i
--arch arm64 --os linux
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
GCC evaluates function call arguments left-to-right on arm64; check that goto
conversion models this: f's side effect (n = n + 1) must take effect before
g's (n = n * 2), giving n == 2. The input is a preprocessed file so that no
target-specific flags are passed to the native preprocessor.
